diff --git a/gpu/CUDA12.md b/gpu/CUDA12.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fc37da9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gpu/CUDA12.md
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# CUDA 12 GPU pipelines
+
+KinFu, KinFu large-scale and people detection no longer require the removed
+CUDA texture-reference API. CUDA 12.8 builds default to `120`; an explicit
+`CUDA_ARCH_BIN` or `CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES` can select another supported GPU.
+For a Blackwell-only build, use:
+
+```
+cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+  -DBUILD_GPU=ON -DBUILD_CUDA=OFF -DCUDA_ARCH_BIN=120 \
+  -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=120 -DBUILD_tools=OFF
+cmake --build build -j16
+```
+
+`BUILD_CUDA` is PCL's separate, older CUDA subsystem, not the GPU subsystem.
+Both the SASS and embedded PTX in this configuration target SM 120.
+
+## Ownership and ordering
+
+* GPU libraries use per-host-thread default streams, including runtime calls
+  made from C++ translation units. Internal synchronization waits for the
+  calling thread's stream, not other trackers or detectors. A host-side active
+  frame count is used only to choose integration tile granularity: isolated
+  frames favor latency, overlapping frames avoid replay overhead. Both execute
+  exactly the same sequence of floating-point additions for every voxel.
+* Image textures are immutable, invocation-owned texture objects. Kernels
+  receive typed handles by value. Owners survive the last stream use, and
+  neither images nor foreground thresholds live in device-global symbols.
+* Marching-cubes lookup tables are instance-owned device arrays, passed as
+  read-only pointers. Cloud/slice extraction and marching-cubes compaction use
+  a count/scan/emit pipeline with warp-sized rows and short z tiles. Integer
+  classification records crossing masks; emission visits only active warps.
+  Scratch arrays are retained by each volume/marching-cubes instance. Prefix
+  sums assign non-overlapping, deterministic output ranges. There is no
+  last-block counter or shared-memory output staging protocol.
+* NCV's active stream is host-thread-local. Haar compaction counters belong to
+  the invocation and participate in NCV's allocator size-counting protocol.
+  The detector's byte-mask dilation runs on its own stream, rather than NPP's
+  process-wide default stream.
+
+## Numerical contracts
+
+* ICP still forms float products and sums them in double precision, using the
+  original binary reduction tree. Warps work on different matrix entries;
+  register shuffles replace the repeated shared-memory reductions. A thread-
+  and device-local CUDA graph submits the two ICP kernels; a pinned asynchronous
+  result copy followed by a stream wait supplies the unchanged CPU solve. The
+  graph is updated with the caller's arrays/pose and completes before reuse.
+* TSDF integration, voxel addressing, ray marching and interpolation formulas
+  are unchanged. Integration is tiled in z, replaying incremental coordinate
+  additions up to each tile boundary; replacing these additions by a multiply
+  would change TSDF quantization.
+* NCV byte integral images read their logical source pointer, including
+  unaligned sources. Linear reads preserve zero-outside-resource behavior,
+  rather than reading guard allocations or repeatedly mirroring tiny ROIs.
+  Hardware texture objects preserve the normalized-coordinate, addressing and
+  fixed-point filtering behavior of resize and frame interpolation.
+* People detection retains seed order, neighbor order, the original hue
+  expression and the seed-relative hue test. The CPU flood fill uses an
+  unvisited bitmap and conservative hue eligibility bitmaps to skip impossible
+  candidates; the original floating-point predicates still decide acceptance.
+  Invalid-component statistics are not accumulated because they are never
+  consumed. Smoothing's otherwise unwritten border is initialized explicitly.
+
+## Validation
+
+Build downstream tools against the installed libraries without changing their
+sources. Exercise both trackers with noisy and noiseless trajectories, color,
+`--api`, repeated extraction, shifting, and mixed concurrent instances. Compare
+all non-timing JSON fields and binary outputs between standalone and concurrent
+runs. People labels and NCV buffers should also agree between normal and
+instrumented execution. Set `OMP_NUM_THREADS=1` for people comparisons.
+
+Run **each** workload under `compute-sanitizer --error-exitcode 1` with each of
+`--tool memcheck`, `--tool racecheck`, and `--tool synccheck`. Include tiny filter
+ROIs, unaligned integral sources, Haar's alternate compaction implementations,
+and a KinFu large-scale trajectory long enough to shift. Do not benchmark while
+another process is running a sanitizer. Check generated architectures with
+`cuobjdump --list-elf` and `cuobjdump --dump-ptx` on the GPU shared libraries.
